# 8. 🚫 Not Everything Deserves Equal Attention

This is where the book challenges conventional productivity thinking.

Traditional thinking:

> "Work harder on everything."

80/20 thinking:

> **"Find what matters most and concentrate there."**

Imagine two students.

### Student A

Studies:

```text
10 subjects × 1 hour
```

### Student B

First identifies:

```text
Most important concepts
Most frequently tested areas
Weakest high-value topics
```

Then concentrates effort accordingly.

Student B is using an **80/20 decision framework**.

