# 9. ⚡ 80/20 and "Less Is More"

The book isn't simply saying:

> "Do 20% of your work."

That would be an oversimplification.

The deeper principle is:

> **Eliminate or reduce low-value activities so that your resources can be concentrated on high-value activities.**

That could mean:

* fewer unnecessary meetings
* fewer low-value commitments
* fewer distractions
* fewer inefficient processes
* fewer unimportant goals

while increasing effort where it actually matters.

