# 13. 🎯 80/20 + Goals

One common mistake is having too many goals.

Imagine:

```text
Learn AI
Learn ML
Learn Cloud
Learn Cybersecurity
Learn DSA
Build projects
Improve English
Prepare aptitude
Prepare interviews
Read books
Exercise
```

Every goal competes for attention.

80/20 thinking asks:

> **Which few goals would create the greatest overall improvement?**

Then concentrate resources there.

This doesn't mean abandoning everything else permanently.

It means **sequencing priorities instead of treating everything as equally urgent**.

