# 15. ⚠️ One Important Limitation

Don't blindly force everything into an 80/20 ratio.

Real-world distributions aren't always exactly 80/20.

The principle is best treated as a **heuristic for finding disproportionate impact**, not as a guarantee.

For example:

> "Exactly 20% of my DSA topics will always produce exactly 80% of my interview questions."

That isn't something you should assume without evidence.

Instead:

> "Let's examine my target companies and past assessments and identify which patterns appear disproportionately often."

That's a much stronger application.

